When the deliverable submitted for a check is an AER-1 receipt, the checker base64-decodes `canonical_bytes` and recomputes SHA-256. If that equals `output_hash`, the criteria are judged against those canonical bytes. The signed record's `files.remediated.sha256` is then the receipt's `output_hash`, so the record names the same bytes the receipt commits to. The record also states the receipt id it was given and the digest of the receipt as submitted.

